      "treatment_summary": "Antiepileptic drugs lamotrigine, oxcarbamazepine, levetiracetam (also in combination) and a short valproate trial (assumed side-effects; epilepsy therapy-resistant); vagus nerve stimulator implantation (followed by weeks without seizures); acetazolamide, attempted replacement by topiramate; currently topiramate and acetazolamide with regular emergency medication; melatonin for sleep disorder.",
      "disease_label_as_stated": "SSADH deficiency (succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase deficiency, SSADHD), severe phenotype",
      "clinical_diagnosis_basis": "Biochemical diagnosis at age two years: increased urinary GHB and γ-butyrolacton on organic acid analysis, elevated CSF GABA and GHB, and absent SSADH enzyme activity in lymphocytes; later Sanger sequencing of the whole ALDH5A1 coding sequence (done as part of a scientific evaluation) showing compound heterozygosity.",
      "source_reference_in_review": "not reported",
      "variants": [
        {
          "gene_symbol_as_stated": "ALDH5A1",
          "variant_original_string": "c.278G > T",
          "transcript_as_stated": "NM_001080.3",
          "cdna_hgvs_as_stated": "c.278G > T",
          "protein_hgvs_as_stated": "p.Cys93Phe",
          "genomic_coordinates_as_stated": null,
          "variant_type_as_stated": "missense",
          "zygosity": "compound heterozygous",
          "inheritance": "not reported",
          "parental_testing_statement": "not reported",
          "functional_evidence_statement": "Reported (ref. [12]) to reduce SSADH enzyme activity to about 3% when expressed in vitro. FoldX: monomer ddG 7.20 kcal/mol; FFFF tetramer 28.09 kcal/mol (destabilizing); mixed tetramers with p.Leu243Pro 26.41-29.09 kcal/mol. Pathogenicity scores: SIFT 0.16, PolyPhen 0.972, REVEL 0.638. In the patient's fibroblasts (carrying both variants): ALDH5A1 mRNA expression no different from two controls; nearly complete absence of SSADH protein on Western blot; complete absence of SSADH enzyme activity in patient lymphocytes.",
          "pathogenicity_as_stated_by_authors": "known pathogenic variant",
          "acmg_criteria_as_stated": "not reported"
        },
        {
          "gene_symbol_as_stated": "ALDH5A1",
          "variant_original_string": "c.728T > C (p.Leu243Pro)",
          "transcript_as_stated": "NM_001080.3",
          "cdna_hgvs_as_stated": "c.728T > C",
          "protein_hgvs_as_stated": "p.Leu243Pro",
          "genomic_coordinates_as_stated": null,
          "variant_type_as_stated": "missense",
          "zygosity": "compound heterozygous",
          "inheritance": "not reported",
          "parental_testing_statement": "not reported",
          "functional_evidence_statement": "Patient fibroblasts (carrying both variants): ALDH5A1 mRNA expression no different from two controls; nearly complete absence of SSADH protein on Western blot. p.Leu243Pro construct transfected into SSADH-KO-HEK-293T cells: no protein expression and enzyme activity only 0.7% of wildtype. FoldX: monomer ddG 7.63 kcal/mol; PPPP tetramer 29.36 kcal/mol (highly destabilizing). Pathogenicity scores: SIFT 0, PolyPhen 0.999, REVEL 0.931. Leu243 conserved in all 30 closest mammalian SSADH sequences.",
          "pathogenicity_as_stated_by_authors": "novel pathogenic missense variant; causative for SSADHD",
          "acmg_criteria_as_stated": "not reported"
        }
